  <ym-title|YM-000026 centered production:
  evidence><label|ym-000026-centered-production-evidence>

  Status: author draft. This unit has not yet received independent
  mathematical or Lean-correspondence review. Source revision inspected:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

  <section|Scope and result><label|scope-and-result>

  The prose is <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-production.tex>. It
  proves the finite-volume weighted coefficient-price bound from the actual
  overlay density expansion, the positive vacuum denominator bound, the
  source pay/coverage scale arithmetic, and two elementary geometric/width
  estimates. The finite-volume transfer/root step is in
  <verbatim|centered-budget.tex>. The multisource lane/birth/raw producer is
  stated as an exact open dependency, not claimed proved here.

  The source does <strong|not> construct the RG stop service records from the
  mere existence of a Wilson history. The finite-volume price result is
  conditional on actual radial lane data. The <verbatim|Fuel.record> scale
  arithmetic is conditional on ready/covering certificates. Construction of
  the physical lanes, their terminal birth estimate, the raw adjacent-scale
  estimates, and the cutoff thickness bound remains a substantive open
  producer task.

  <section|Correspondence><label|correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  passage>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned source>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence and
  scope>>>|<row|<cell|Weighted absolute price and
  exponential>|<cell|<verbatim|Poly.price>, <verbatim|Poly.toll>,
  <verbatim|Poly.pass_budget>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Marker/Truncated.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|price_w>
  is the weighted sum of absolute monomial coefficients, with weight the
  product of marker weights. The mode product is disjoint union and is zero
  on overlapping marker sets, so every positive-degree element is nilpotent
  of degree at most $>>|<row|<cell|Density
  decomposition>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Overlay.Bands.extra>, <verbatim|.each>,
  <verbatim|.packet>, <verbatim|.cluster>, <verbatim|.density>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Table.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|extra> is the sum of
  local unit monomials and positive-ray monomials. <verbatim|each> is the
  vacuum activity plus the sum of marked interactions. <verbatim|packet> is
  the product over a finite set of site indices, zeroed when inadmissible;
  <verbatim|cluster> sums these packets. <verbatim|density> multiplies the
  completed-algebra pass of <verbatim|extra> and <verbatim|cluster> by the
  scalar Wilson exponential. The article's
  <math|E<rsub|0>,E<rsub|<math-up|add>>,C> are these three factors. Its full
  squarefree marker algebra is the actual <verbatim|Overlay.census>
  specialization used by <verbatim|Overlay.Supplier>/<verbatim|Overlay.Terminal>;
  the more general <verbatim|Console.Census> may be downward-restricted. The
  additional exponent has zero quiet component because unit/ray marker
  supports are nonempty; ray coefficients are masked to zero off healthy
  support.>>|<row|<cell|Radial prices>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Overlay.Bands.Active>,
  <verbatim|.Radial>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Table.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|proper>
  and <verbatim|occurs> assert each positive ray/marked support is nonempty.
  <verbatim|localU> bounds the toll-weighted unit. <verbatim|bulk> bounds
  rays on healthy support and gives a per-origin support-mass budget (c).
  <verbatim|hits> bounds marked coefficients and gives a per-origin
  forced-support budget (d b); article notation uses (gamma b_0) for this
  product. The vacuum activity need not be nonnegative:
  <verbatim|Activities.Valid.boundK> gives a nonnegative summable majorant of
  its absolute value, with per-site price budget
  <math|\<kappa\>>.>>|<row|<cell|Summing origins and the subset
  series>|<cell|<verbatim|Bands.per_system>, <verbatim|.bulkBound>,
  <verbatim|.baseBound>, <verbatim|.population>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Pays.lean>>|<cell|For any family with nonempty
  supports, every term occurs in at least one origin sum; summing the (q)
  origin budgets bounds its total charge by (q) times the per-origin budget.
  <verbatim|.bulkBound> adds the local cost (q u), producing (q(u+c)).
  <verbatim|.baseBound> gives total activity cost (s_0\\kappa+q\\gamma b_0),
  where (s_0) is the site count. <verbatim|.population> bounds the admissible
  subset sum by the unrestricted product (prod_i(1+f_i)\\leq e^{\\sum_i
  f_i}); the infinite-index passage uses summability and monotone finite
  truncations.>>|<row|<cell|Pointwise and integrated
  numerator>|<cell|<verbatim|Bands.physical>, <verbatim|.material>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Bill.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lawful.exponentEnv>
  supplies the upper bound (E_0\\leq scalar+s_0,exCost). Pointwise price
  therefore has exponent (scalar+s_0(exCost+\\kappa)+q(u+c+\\gamma b_0)). A
  coefficient's toll times its absolute value is at most the full absolute
  price. Integrating against the probability prior preserves this bound;
  measurability is provided by <verbatim|density_meas> and
  lawfulness.>>|<row|<cell|Vacuum denominator>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.RG.calm>,
  <verbatim|.voids>, <verbatim|.space>, <verbatim|PathData.under>,
  <verbatim|Rep.exponent_lo>, <verbatim|.denominator>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Vac/Shelter.lean>>|<cell|Restrict to the event that every
  oriented edge lies in the gauge ball of radius (s/4). The four-edge
  plaquette path has chord at most (s), so flags vanish for (s\\leq
  threshold). The local path/plaquette action is at most the per-site loop
  cost plus (\\beta,baseBudget(s)), by <verbatim|PathData.under>. On this
  event <verbatim|exponent_lo> bounds the integrand below by
  (e^{scalar-s_0(exCost+\\beta baseBudget(s))}). The product-prior measure is
  at least $(s/16)^{d_G>>|<row|<cell|Normalized
  price>|<cell|<verbatim|Bands.total>, <verbatim|YM.Overlay.Lane.pays>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Bill.lean>, <verbatim|Engine.lean>>|<cell|Dividing
  the numerator estimate by the positive denominator gives the exact
  <verbatim|finalBill>: <math|s<rsub|0>*<around|(|2*<space|0.17em>e*x*C*o*s*t+\<kappa\>+\<beta\>*<space|0.17em>b*a*s*e*B*u*d*g*e*t<around|(|s|)>+4*d<rsub|G>*log
  <around|(|16/s|)>|)>+q*<around|(|u+c+\<gamma\>*b<rsub|0>|)>>.
  <verbatim|Lane.pays> applies this to a transfer lane after finite iteration
  of its transfer recursion.>>|<row|<cell|Separated-support
  price>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.I01.answer>, <verbatim|Corona.ring_path>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/I01.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Corona/Fit.lean>>|<cell|The
  prose gives the full constants: the ring traversal length obeys
  <math|N\<leqslant\>D*<around|(|4*B+2|)>>; visit times for pairwise
  <math|B<rsup|2>>-separated markers differ by at least <math|B<rsup|2>-2*B>;
  for <math|B\<geqslant\>8> and at least two markers this yields
  $>>|<row|<cell|Sublinear width price>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.I04.columns_receipt>,
  <verbatim|.hat_receipt>, <verbatim|.answer>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/I04.lean>>|<cell|The prose proves the finite-prefix
  telescoping from the exact source increment gate <math|log
  c<rsub|i+1>\<leqslant\><around|(|\<epsilon\>/2|)>*<around|(|\<sigma\><rsub|i+1>-\<sigma\><rsub|i>|)>>.
  The source derives that gate from <verbatim|Levels.fits.logCost>;
  <verbatim|.hat_receipt> gives <math|log
  <wide|\<beta\>|^><rsub|i>=o<around|(|\<sigma\><rsub|i>|)>>, and the
  factorial budget gives <math|log <around|(|\<nu\><rsub|i>!|)>\<leqslant\>log
  c<rsub|i>>. These imply the stated width bill <math|5-log
  w<rsub|i>=o<around|(|\<sigma\><rsub|i>|)>>.>>|<row|<cell|Stopping-level
  treasury>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Vac.treasury>, <verbatim|.suffices_bill>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Vac/Treasury.lean>>|<cell|The represented history has
  actual inverse coupling at most <math|2*<wide|\<beta\>|^><rsub|r>>. The
  loop price is monotone in this coupling; the base-budget term is
  nonnegative and monotone. Hence <verbatim|finalBill> is at most the number
  of stopping-torus sites times <verbatim|treasury(r)>, plus the marker toll
  cost. The four-dimensional site identity is
  <math|s<rsub|0>=n*<around|(|a<rsub|m>/a<rsub|r>|)><rsup|4>>. Thus
  <math|\<tau\><rsub|r>=t*r*e*a*s*u*r*y<around|(|r|)>>, with
  <math|\<beta\><rsub|r>=2*<wide|\<beta\>|^><rsub|r>>.>>|<row|<cell|Price/pay
  and coverage to bill>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Stock.Fuel.ready>,
  <verbatim|.covers>, <verbatim|.record>; <verbatim|Tabs.chosen>,
  <verbatim|.pay>; <verbatim|YM.Vac.treasury_stage>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Prior.lean>, <verbatim|Treasury.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Tabs.chosen>
  selects an opened scale (p(i)\\geq i). Its pay estimate gives
  ((a_i/a_{p(i)})^4,fiat_{p(i)}\\leq z,scale(p(i))) eventually for every
  (z\<gtr\>0). <verbatim|treasury_stage> gives (treasury\\leq fiat), and
  <verbatim|covers> gives the residual marker price at most (z,scale(p(i))).
  Since (fiat\\geq1), (\\log(a_i/a_{p(i)})\\leq(a_i/a_{p(i)})^4 fiat);
  combining the three inequalities yields (bill_i\\leq(g+\\eta)scale(i)), by
  the explicit choice and case split in the prose. <verbatim|ready> and the
  schedule opening condition give service at the selected scale, so
  <verbatim|record> returns the stop-indexed services and eventual
  bill.>>|<row|<cell|Exact missing RG/multisource
  production>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Source.Family.Makes>;
  <verbatim|YM.Extra.Multi.Prepared>; <verbatim|YM.Extra.Multi.Thick>;
  <verbatim|YM.Extra.Multi.Offer>; <verbatim|YM.Mix.Unbilled>,
  <verbatim|.Raw>; <verbatim|YM.Extra.Multi.System.Forward.step>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Source/Construction.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/MULTISOURCE_BOUNDS/{Schedule,Trajectory,Step,Application}.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Makes>
  supplies the actual family/cylinder, locality/covariance/reality,
  order/reference/stencil and priced-section data. <verbatim|Prepared>
  requires Tabs, factorial columns, per-scale atlas, adjacent steepness and
  block shape; <verbatim|Schedule.pricing> obtains it only from paid
  numerical gates. <verbatim|Thick> separately requires a nonnegative
  summable majorant <math|k<rsub|i>> for $>>|<row|<cell|Higher producer
  obligations>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Input.Metered.rootwise>,
  <verbatim|YM.Extra.Multi.metered>, <verbatim|YM.Stock.Stops.centering>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Assembly.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/MULTISOURCE_BOUNDS/Application.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Supplier.lean>>|<cell|This file does not prove
  <verbatim|Fuel.ready> or <verbatim|Fuel.covers>. The multisource
  construction requires its stated <verbatim|Makes>,
  <verbatim|Prepared>/factorial and tab inputs, eventual thickness, offer,
  and gauge simplicity conditions. The output of <verbatim|Fuel.record> is
  then consumed by <verbatim|Stops.centering> to produce <verbatim|Wcmain>.
  These are explicit upstream prerequisites, not consequences of the density
  price lemma.>>>>>

  <section|Limits and open dependency><label|limits-and-open-dependency>

  The radial lane estimate is proved, but its hypotheses are substantive: a
  lane must exist at each relevant slab with common uniform radial budgets.
  Likewise, the eventual stop records require ready and coverage predicates.
  More fundamentally, the offered lanes already assume raw one-step
  estimates, and the terminal birth argument assumes thickness.
  <verbatim|Forward.step> is an optional conditional route to the raw
  estimate; its upstream component and integration hypotheses are not
  established from the gauge setup here. The next producer unit must trace
  actual callers of <verbatim|Offer>, <verbatim|Unbilled.Raw>, and
  <verbatim|Thick> back from the final supplier, prove the available upstream
  estimates, and mark any still-open analytic premises explicitly.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Inspected the listed declarations and immediate dependencies at the
    pinned source revision; no Lean files were edited.

    <item>A combined <verbatim|latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode
    -halt-on-error> build of centered-estimates, centered-budget, and
    centered-production succeeded after the latest prose edits (15-page PDF
    in <verbatim|/tmp/ym-centered-build>).

    <item>No Lean build was run.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run and stopped
    because <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> is missing from
    this checkout; metadata is outside the owned outputs.

    <item>Independent review is pending.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Integrated local review><label|integrated-local-review>

  The independent stronger-agent conditional pass is recorded in
  <verbatim|reviews/draft-review.md>; all machine review fields remain null.
  The earlier pending-review entries above record the author checkout stage.
  Actual lane, terminal birth, raw-step and service producers remain
  obligations.

